    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d457">

                <pb facs="0878" n="860" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg860"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Department of State Atomic Energy Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. George F. Kennan to the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-18">July 18, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Acheson</hi>: The demands of my new job with the
                    War College have forced me to study a good deal of the basic material on the
                    problem of the international control of atomic energy.</p>
                <pb facs="0879" n="861" xml:id="pg861"/>
                <p>To clarify my own thoughts on the position of the USSR with relation to this
                    subject, I have written them out in the form of a few questions and answers.</p>
                <p>I thought you might find these of interest, and attach a copy.</p>
                <p>I am off for a speaking tour in the far west, and will be back in the end of
                    August.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Kennan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d457-a1.xml" xpointer="d457-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
